# @badabhai/admin-web — internal admin portal (ADR-0025, 4th auth principal).
# Copy to .env.local for local dev. NEVER commit a real secret.

# --- Server-only (never reaches the client bundle) ---
# The internal API origin. Deliberately NOT NEXT_PUBLIC_* — the browser must never learn
# it, and no admin request is ever made from the client (every call goes through a server
# action or server component using adminFetch). Defaults to http://localhost:3001 here for
# local dev ONLY — there is no non-local default baked into the app.
#
# DEPLOYING A NEW ENVIRONMENT (staging/production): set this to that environment's real
# `apps/api` origin. If it is left unset, every server-side API call — including the
# dashboard's own health probe — silently targets http://localhost:3001, which does not
# exist off a dev box, and every request fails. The portal will not tell you why: the
# underlying fetch error is deliberately suppressed in `src/lib/admin-http.ts` (it can
# contain the internal API origin), so what you will actually see is a generic
# "The admin API is unreachable." on every page. Treat that message as step one of this
# checklist, not as a backend outage.
ADMIN_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3001

# --- Public (shipped to the browser; NEXT_PUBLIC_* only) ---
# Environment label. Set to "staging" (or "production") to mark the session cookie
# `Secure` (HTTPS-only) on a deployed https host. Local http dev stays non-secure.
NEXT_PUBLIC_ENVIRONMENT=development
# The canonical public origin of this portal (used for absolute URLs where needed).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3003
